 ") used instead of the equality operator (",
 ButtonBox["==",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/Equal.html"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/Equal.html"],
 "), corrected the code, and explained the wave equation and its initial and \
boundary conditions despite the imperfect prompt."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  4.0030543618590355`*^9, 4.003236136634411*^9, {4.0032362263857346`*^9, 
   4.0032362263866997`*^9}, {4.0032362596155853`*^9, 
   4.003236259616583*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9c908614-890f-864c-88df-\
918436d4899e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Complete Notebook Project", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.003054917690548*^9, 
  4.0030549208114834`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f97cae2b-a654-d14c-aec9-\
f15e0d8ac604"],

Cell["\<\
In this task, you will ask the assistant to build a complete educational \
notebook from scratch. The project explains a simple pendulum\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s small-angle motion through mathematics, executable code, \
plots, and a synchronized animation. Use the following prompt:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  4.0030549333929863`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"4ce47d27-4547-1149-95c2-\
b38ac60730ef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Create and open a complete, self-contained Wolfram notebook explaining \
simple harmonic motion using a pendulum, suitable for high-school students. \
Use exactly \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Pendulum SHM\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] as \
both the notebook\[CloseCurlyQuote]s title cell and window title. Define SHM \
as \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]simple harmonic motion\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] in \
the introduction. Organize the notebook into numbered sections, each with a \
brief explanation. Immediately before every executable input cell, include a \
separate descriptive caption using the actual \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]CodeText\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] cell style. Start each caption with an imperative \
verb and end it with a colon. Display the main equations clearly on separate \
lines. Include:\n1. The physical system and assumptions: a point mass \
attached to a massless rigid support of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["L", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4520b015-1755-f946-bff8-9c97ba21feb2"],
 ", a fixed pivot, no friction or air resistance, and a small initial angle.\n\
2. A concise mathematical explanation starting from the exact pendulum \
equation and deriving the small-angle equation for simple harmonic motion. \
Define all symbols and use radians in the equations.\n3. Code that constructs \
and solves the approximate equation for a pendulum released from rest.\n4. A \
plot of angular displacement against time, with labeled axes and units.\n5. A \
smooth animation showing a fixed pivot, visible support, and bob, \
synchronized with a moving point on the angular displacement\[Dash]time \
graph.\n6. A short explanation of the period and its dependence on pendulum \
length and gravitational acceleration.\n\nUse ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"L", "=", 
    RowBox[{"1", " ", 
     StyleBox["m",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "55e01b80-8229-724e-8c98-ea23d51db199"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"g", "=", 
    RowBox[{"9.81", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["m",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], "/", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["s",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5d8f20c6-bfb2-0349-b5e3-9db24f30a571"],
 ", and an initial angle of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["10", "\[Degree]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "aef91610-dfa0-bc40-9cda-794d81505151"],
 ", converted to radians in the code. Clearly distinguish the exact pendulum \
equation from its small-angle approximation. Keep the explanations, \
mathematics, and code concise and accessible. Initialize all variables so \
that all input cells can be evaluated in order from top to bottom in a fresh \
kernel session. Ensure that the solution is correctly evaluated as a function \
of time and that the animation uses the specified pendulum length. Use a \
consistent, readable layout throughout the notebook."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  4.0030576073308926`*^9, {4.0030586212888546`*^9, 4.003058636379484*^9}, {
   4.0032240958462887`*^9, 
   4.0032241794387474`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"447abbb1-b776-4849-9fa7-\
3739c263a990"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Open the assistant-generated pendulum project in ",
 ButtonBox["Wolfram Cloud",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://www.wolframcloud.com/"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://www.wolframcloud.com/"],
 ". Sign in with your Wolfram ID if required:"
}], "CodeText",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0030591462924633`*^9, 4.0030591616951084`*^9}, {
  4.0032217404911575`*^9, 
  4.0032217404921455`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cf036b6c-0376-bc46-a65b-\
1c1396827ec6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"SystemOpen", 
  "[", "\"\<https://www.wolframcloud.com/env/akram_2007_omar/Zewail%20Seminar/\
Pendulum%20SHM.nb\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0030582509975376`*^9, 4.0030582509975376`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[24]:=",ExpressionUUID->"8ea008fa-0fa6-3848-b8e8-df10b16ef5f6"],

Cell["\<\
Alternatively, open the assistant-generated project embedded in this seminar \
notebook in a separate window:\
\>", "CodeText",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.003059173500349*^9, 
  4.0030591865824738`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"94e9ad30-623b-f844-a420-\
30ab037b90a7"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"NotebookPut", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"CurrentValue", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"EvaluationNotebook", "[", "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"TaggingRules", ",", "\"\<PendulumSHM\>\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"WindowTitle", "->", "\"\<Pendulum SHM\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0030587290394993`*^9, 4.0030587290394993`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[25]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ad9d84d5-6de9-2843-983c-4313cbb5e07e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TemplateBox[<|
  "obj" -> NotebookObject[
    "3ba5014f-eb07-f240-97bf-1125d8f0b7bf", 
     "e451b8a4-f8dc-0a45-af96-dfebc6fd5645"], "label" -> "\"Pendulum SHM\""|>,
  "NotebookObjectUUIDsUnsaved"]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.003412593599003*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[25]=",ExpressionUUID->"0cfacf65-4326-7b40-b639-53944ae73be8"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Visualization and Interactivity", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0030396183752174`*^9, 4.00303962213538*^9}, 
   4.0030697627017384`*^9, {4.0030718876905727`*^9, 4.0030718941337967`*^9}, {
   4.003071993262148*^9, 4.003071994892153*^9}, 4.0030882247146397`*^9, {
   4.0030882883324375`*^9, 4.00308828880929*^9}, 
   4.0034994775471*^9},ExpressionUUID->"4c0f94e1-580b-6046-905a-95b10ff8883c"],

Cell["\<\
Turn equations, text, and computational results into interactive experiences. \
Explore oscillations with adjustable controls, uncover patterns in text, \
publish a web application, and visualize physical systems in motion.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  4.0031537341760273`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"6b88c856-a2c6-3542-af7b-\
51cac988bd5e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Simple Harmonic Motion", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.984129082398199*^9, 3.9841290848348694`*^9}, 
   3.9841349148902054`*^9, 4.003068882612812*^9, {4.003150179535412*^9, 
